; Regression (R1, 2026-09-19): a call into ANOTHER PACKAGE's non-generic body
; reaches the planner as a stub, which carries no `mutable` marks and is always
; a procedure. The gate read that as "writes nothing", so a function could
; write its parameter through StringBuilder.append without a word. A stub is
; judged by the Model's declarations of its owner, name and arity now.
; xfail: error: function sneaky_append writes what its parameters reach (sb:ref[StringBuilder])

function sneaky_append(sb: ref[StringBuilder]) returns int
{
    sb.append "x"
    0
}

var b StringBuilder()
let r sneaky_append(&b)
print "`r`\n"
